    "title": "pandas.Timedelta.value — pandas 3.1.0.dev0+1662.g0c49719283 documentation",
    "status": 200,
    "markdown": "# pandas.Timedelta.value#\n\n- Timedelta.value#\n- Return the value of Timedelta object in nanoseconds. Return the total seconds, milliseconds and microseconds of the timedelta as nanoseconds. \n  - Returns:\n    - int\n See also \n  - `Timedelta.unit`\n  - Return the unit of Timedelta object.\n Examples >>> pd.Timedelta(1, \"us\").value 1000",
